{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:10.1126/science.167.3926.1740","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"5416541","source":"MED","pmid":"5416541","doi":"10.1126/science.167.3926.1740","title":"Habituation and dishabituation of the gill-withdrawal reflex in Aplysia.","authorString":"Pinsker H, Kupfermann I, Castellucci V, Kandel E.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Pinsker H","lastName":"Pinsker","firstName":"H","initials":"H"},{"fullName":"Kupfermann I","lastName":"Kupfermann","firstName":"I","initials":"I"},{"fullName":"Castellucci V","lastName":"Castellucci","firstName":"V","initials":"V"},{"fullName":"Kandel E","lastName":"Kandel","firstName":"E","initials":"E"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3926","volume":"167","journalIssueId":1459476,"dateOfPublication":"1970 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":1970,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Science","title":"Science (New York, N.Y.)","essn":"1095-9203","issn":"0036-8075","isoabbreviation":"Science","nlmid":"0404511"},"printPublicationDate":"1970-03-01"},"pubYear":"1970","pageInfo":"1740-1742","abstractText":"A behavioral reflex mediated by identified motor neurons in the abdominal ganglion of Aplysia undergoes two simple forms of shortterm modification. When the gill-with-drawal reflex was repeatedly evoked by a tactile stimulus to the siphon or mantle shelf, the amplitude of the response showed marked decrement (habituation). After a period of rest the response showed spontaneous recovery. The amplitude of a habituated response was facilitated by the presentation of a strong tactile stimulus to another part of the animal (dishabituation). Many characteristics of habituation and dishabituation in Aplysia are similar to those in vertebrates.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Motor Neurons","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gills","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mollusca","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Reflex"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Touch"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Habituation, Psychophysiologic"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.167.3926.1740"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":211,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"1970-04-14","dateOfCreation":"1970-03-27","dateOfRevision":"2019-06-18","firstPublicationDate":"1970-03-01","firstIndexDate":"2009-10-28","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}